    "partNumber": 4,
    "formContent": "<div class=\"ielts-form-container\"><div class=\"form-section\"><div class=\"form-title\" style=\"text-align:center;font-weight:700;font-size:1.1em;margin-bottom:8px;\">Music therapy for surgical patients</div><p style=\"font-weight:700;\">Background</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; Surgery impacts patients because they may experience discomfort or unwelcome changes to their <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"31\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> .</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; Current post-surgical strategies focus mainly on pain relief.</p><p style=\"font-weight:700;margin-top:10px;\">Recent research</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; A study reviewed data from about 100 <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"32\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> and found that listening to music</p><p style=\"padding-left:42px;\">improved hospital patients&rsquo; sense of wellbeing.</p><p style=\"padding-left:42px;\">reduced the length of their stay.</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; The patients in the study all listened to music with a <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"33\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> effect.</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; The music was mostly played through music <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"34\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> .</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; Patients reported an absence or low levels of <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"35\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> .</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; Medical records confirmed that patients who were played music in hospital needed less <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"36\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> than those who weren&rsquo;t played music.</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; The best results were achieved when patients were played music while they were <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"37\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> .</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; The study concluded that playing music was effective because it served as a <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"38\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> .</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; The researchers recommend playing either music or sounds from <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"39\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> to all surgical patients.</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; A future study will investigate the best <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"40\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> for the music.</p></div></div>",
    "instruction": "You will hear part of a lecture to medical students about music therapy for surgical patients.<br>Complete the notes below. Write <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> for each answer.",
